{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T06:57:49Z","content":"Here is how to run either project in **Visual Studio Code**:\n\n---\n\n## 1. How to Run the Web App in VS Code\n\n### Step 1: Open the Folder\n1. Open **Visual Studio Code**.\n2. Click **File** > **Open Folder...** (or press `Ctrl + K, Ctrl + O`).\n3. Select this folder:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\offline-password-manager\n   ```\n\n### Step 2: Open the Terminal in VS Code\n* Press **`Ctrl + \\``** (the backtick key under Escape), or click **Terminal** > **New Terminal** at the top.\n\n### Step 3: Run the Commands\n1. Type this and press **Enter** (first time only to install React & Vite):\n   ```bash\n   npm install\n   ```\n2. Then start the local server:\n   ```bash\n   npm run dev\n   ```\n3. Hold **`Ctrl` and click** the link in the terminal:\n   ```text\n   http://localhost:3000\n   ```\nThe web app will open in your browser!\n\n---\n\n## 2. How to Run the Browser Extension in VS Code\n\nA one-click debug configuration has been set up for the extension:\n\n### Step 1: Open the Extension Folder\n1. In VS Code, click **File** > **Open Folder...**\n2. Select:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\offline-vault-extension\n   ```\n\n### Step 2: Press F5 (One-Click Run)\n1. Press **`F5`** on your keyboard (or click **Run** > **Start Debugging**).\n2. Choose **\"Launch Chrome with Extension\"** or **\"Launch Edge with Extension\"**.\n3. VS Code will automatically:\n   - Launch a new browser window.\n   - Automatically load the **Offline Vault extension** with auto-fill enabled.\n   - Open **GitHub login** so you can test it immediately!"}
