{"step_index":123,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T07:03:12Z","content":"Here are the **3 things you can do right now**:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Test Logging into GitHub Right Now (Manual Copy)\n1. On your screen, look at the **Password** line:\n   ```text\n   Password  ••••••••••  👁  📋\n   ```\n2. Click the **Copy icon (📋)** — it will copy your password to your clipboard.\n3. Click the blue link **`github.com ↗`** to open GitHub in a new tab.\n4. On GitHub, paste (`Ctrl + V`) into the password field to log in!\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Turn on Automatic Auto-Fill (So it fills GitHub automatically)\nIf you want GitHub to **automatically show the auto-fill button** (without needing to copy/paste manually):\n1. In this same browser, open a new tab and go to:\n   - If using Chrome: `chrome://extensions`\n   - If using Edge: `edge://extensions`\n2. Turn ON **\"Developer mode\"** (toggle in the top right).\n3. Click **\"Load unpacked\"** (top left button) and select this folder:\n   ```text\n   C:\\Users\\vijay\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\offline-vault-extension\n   ```\n4. Now when you go to **https://github.com/login**, a green shield icon (🛡️) will appear right inside the GitHub login box for 1-click auto-fill!\n\n---\n\n### Option 3: Fix the Red \"Health (1)\" Alert\nNotice the red badge at the top: **`🛡️ Health (1)`**:\n* Click on **Health** — the vault detected that your GitHub password might be too short or weak.\n* Click **\"✨ Generator\"** in the top bar to see how you can generate an unbreakable 20-character password.","thinking":"**Interpreting User's Next Step**\n\nThe user has the web application open and has added a single entry. The question \"now what to do\" likely indicates they're ready to proceed beyond basic manual entry. It's likely that the user needs the next feature (automatic password saving). The agent needs to guide the user towards that feature.\n\n\n"}
